{"id":"CVE-2012-2110","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2012-04-19T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T19:26:07.655Z","description":"The asn1_d2i_read_bio function in crypto/asn1/a_d2i_fp.c in OpenSSL before 0.9.8v, 1.0.0 before 1.0.0i, and 1.0.1 before 1.0.1a does not properly interpret integer data, which allows remote attackers to conduct buffer overflow attacks, and cause a denial of service (memory corruption) or possibly have unspecified other impact, via crafted DER data, as demonstrated by an X.509 certificate or an RSA public key.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2012-05/msg00014.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SU-2012:0623"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2012-09/msg00007.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SU-2012:1149"},{"url":"http://www-01.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=ssg1S1004564","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://h20564.www2.hp.com/portal/site/hpsc/public/kb/docDisplay?docId=emr_na-c03839862","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"SSRT101210"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2012-November/092905.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2012-18035"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/48899","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"48899"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/fulldisclosure/2012-04/0209.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20120419 incorrect integer conversions in OpenSSL can result in memory corruption."},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-1308.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:1308"},{"url":"http://cvs.openssl.org/chngview?cn=22434","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.man